  "id": "long-term-memory",
  "term": "long-term memory",
  "definition": "Long-term memory is the capacity to encode, store, and later retrieve information over time. It includes verbal and visuospatial forms, and its performance depends in part on attention, control of interference, and working-memory processes that support remembering.",
